swer/value "-\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306432} {:answer/id #uuid "cbb84485-de1d-5e28-8db9-6dd19e74fb01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{22}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307039}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8655b150-d9ac-58ab-a418-1f5955cc359f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306432} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cfd5eef-81cc-5e6a-a564-ac436e494498" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307965} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cac773e-e4ed-5ac3-adf5-7bb347e54e69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305260} {:answer/id #uuid "2d9f2d2d-2ea2-5856-9ae0-79d1caeb78a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305587} {:answer/id #uuid "ade6f811-e61c-566b-bf55-bd3242070f7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ade6f811-e61c-566b-bf55-bd3242070f7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306793} :answer-field/id #uuid "af31c1c1-2dd8-55ed-bf10-fb67b8f44234" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308079} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6764c333-ac48-5bd0-87a4-f4aa27d7f22d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{64}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306137} {:answer/id #uuid "8dd3e137-38a3-5d3c-a63d-f3d10221d64e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306497} {:answer/id #uuid "b1466641-3f54-5502-936d-c71d4b1571c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{64}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306816}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1466641-3f54-5502-936d-c71d4b1571c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{64}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306816} :answer-field/id #uuid "c46b939e-cfe3-5c22-93ac-38f98d2247ff" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308136}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "66a1a093-337b-53cf-882b-9b2291b3a919" :question/math-academy-id "q-333372" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2xy,\\,y(0)=-1\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using the $2$-step Adams-Bashforth-Moulton method. Given that the step size is $Δx=1,$ and that one preliminary step has already been computed using the Runge-Kutta method, complete the next row of the table below.\n\n*Hint: The corrector equation of the two-step Adams-Bashforth-Moulton method is defined as*\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{12}(5{y}_{p}^{′}+8{y}^{′}-{y}_{-1}^{′})\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\n*where ${y}_{p}$ denotes the predictor at the current step, and ${y}_{-1}^{′}$ is the estimated slope at the previous point.* \n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{5}{3}$ |\n| $1$ | $-\\frac{8}{3}$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} |\n\nTherefore, $y(2)≈$\n  {{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe $2$-Step Adams-Bashforth-Moulton (ABM2) method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Predictor} & : & Δ{y}_{p} & =\\frac{1}{2}(3{y}^{′}-{y}_{-1}^{′})\\cdot Δx, \\\\ \\text{Corrector} & : & Δy & =\\frac{1}{12}(5{y}_{p}^{′}+8{y}^{′}-{y}_{-1}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- ${y}^{′}=f(x,y)$ is the estimated slope at the current point $(x,y),$\n\n- ${y}_{-1}^{′}=f({x}_{-1},{y}_{-1})$ is the estimated slope at the previous point (${x}_{-1},{y}_{-1}),$ and\n\n- ${y}_{p}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{p})$ is the estimated slope at the predicted new point $({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{p})=(x+Δx,y+Δ{y}_{p}).$\n\nWe're told that the first step is calculated using the Runge-Kutta Method, resulting in \n\n$$\ny(1)≈-\\frac{8}{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, we'll continue from this point, using the $2$-step ABM method.\n\nFirst, we compute the value of ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =2xy \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1\\cdot (-\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{16}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{5}{3}$ |\n| $1$ | $-\\frac{8}{3}$ | $-\\frac{16}{3}$ |  |  |  |  |\n\nFrom the first row of the table, we see that the slope at the previous point $({x}_{-1},{y}_{-1})=(0,-1)$ is ${y}_{-1}^{′}=0.$\n\nNext, we compute $Δ{y}_{p}$ using the predictor equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{y}_{p} & =\\frac{1}{2}(3{y}^{′}-{y}_{-1}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(3\\cdot (-\\frac{16}{3})-0)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{5}{3}$ |\n| $1$ | $-\\frac{8}{3}$ | $-\\frac{16}{3}$ | $-8$ |  |  |  |\n\nSo, the coordinates of the predicted new point are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=1+1=2, \\\\ {y}_{p} & =y+Δ{y}_{p}=-\\frac{8}{3}+(-8)=-\\frac{32}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's add the second value to the table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{5}{3}$ |\n| $1$ | $-\\frac{8}{3}$ | $-\\frac{16}{3}$ | $-8$ | $-\\frac{32}{3}$ |  |  |\n\nHence, the slope at this predicted point is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & =2{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{p} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2\\cdot (-\\frac{32}{3}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{128}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{5}{3}$ |\n| $1$ | $-\\frac{8}{3}$ | $-\\frac{16}{3}$ | $-8$ | $-\\frac{32}{3}$ | $-\\frac{128}{3}$ |  |\n\nFinally, we compute $Δy$ using the corrector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{12}(5{y}_{p}^{′}+8{y}^{′}-{y}_{-1}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(5\\cdot (-\\frac{128}{3})+8\\cdot (-\\frac{16}{3})-0)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot (-256) \\\\  & =-\\frac{64}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed row is as given below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{5}{3}$ |\n| $1$ | $-\\frac{8}{3}$ | $-\\frac{16}{3}$ | $-8$ | $-\\frac{32}{3}$ | $-\\frac{128}{3}$ | $-\\frac{64}{3}$ |\n\nThe value of $x$ in the next row is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=2.$ To get the value of $y$ in the next row, we add $Δy$ to $y:$\n\n$$\n{y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy=-\\frac{8}{3}+(-\\frac{64}{3})=-24\n$$\n\nAdding these results to our table gives the following:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}^{′}$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{5}{3}$ |\n| $1$ | $-\\frac{8}{3}$ | $-\\frac{16}{3}$ | $-8$ | $-\\frac{32}{3}$ | $-\\frac{128}{3}$ | $-\\frac{64}{3}$ |\n| $2$ | $-24$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(2)≈-24.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308448 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b5422e4-c19d-5eee-b111-076b88763d27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{41}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305876} {:answer/id #uuid "62a37e6e-422f-56ac-afda-578e98f087e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{39}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306106} {:answer/id #uuid "b01aa469-2412-5018-8fe8-8eb49c67a642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{43}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b5422e4-c19d-5eee-b111-076b88763d27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{41}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305876} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a25d7d8-2ad9-51c5-b7a6-eeac9c455115" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307606} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4122039b-71c6-539c-97d2-9bbfae1e2ac4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305792} {:answer/id #uuid "958e0a82-8dbd-5e87-ac5f-facfca03f825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306557} {:answer/id #uuid "af4a2dbe-1f47-5f00-9c9c-9ad7d805eb8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4122039b-71c6-539c-97d2